# What never belongs in the API image's build context.
#
# The context is the repo root because the image needs api/, src/, config/ and
# scripts/. Everything else is either enormous or irrelevant, and the context is
# uploaded to the daemon before a single layer is built: with data/ in it, that
# upload alone is 26.5 GB.

# Data is a volume, never a layer (api/Dockerfile says why).
data/
outputs/
outputs.zip

# The web app has its own image, built from ./web with its own .dockerignore.
web/
# ...except this one file, which the API reads: BENCHMARK_JSON in api/main.py is
# `web/data/benchmark_vs_bet365.json`. Excluding all of web/ left the API serving
# `benchmark: null`, and the results page -- whose type said the field could not
# be null -- threw while `next build` prerendered it, so the WEB image could not
# be built either. 1.9 KB. Found 2026-11-03 by building the containers.
!web/data/

# Local environments and caches.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
soccerdata_cache/
*.joblib

# Repository plumbing and session scratch.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/
*.log
*.log.stderr

# Documentation and the test suite: CI runs the suite from a checkout, the
# container does not.
docs/
tests/
